# UNVERIFIED — pending debrief
# Defect 2225, panel 230's R3, 2026-10-26: a `.must()` on a `fail` whose message
# held a line feed printed a second line, `panic: integer overflow`, which a
# person and every instrument read as a second abort of another class. A
# program's message is written as the compiler's diagnostics write program text,
# every character a line cannot show by its code, and since this sitting the
# line feed and the tab too (panel 192's R7 had left both as themselves).

function check(n: i64) -> i64?
    if n > 0
        return fail(code: "bad", msg: "x\ty\npanic: integer overflow")
    return ok(n)

function main()
    print(check(1).must())
